<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Zemio</h1><p class="st-meta">1870 CE – 1913 CE (approx.) · capital Zemio</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Zande sultanate on the upper Mbomou whose ruler Zemio allied with Egyptian Sudan and later with Belgian and French officers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Zemio, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zande-people">Zande</a> prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avungara">Vungara dynasty</a>, established his authority on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbomou-river">Mbomou</a> in the 1870s. He built his power in alliance with the administration of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/turco-egyptian-sudan">Egyptian Sudan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahr-al-ghazal">Bahr al-Ghazal</a>, receiving guns in exchange for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Zemio ruled through armed followers and tribute from subject communities, and his court hosted European travellers such as the explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-junker">Wilhelm Junker</a>. After the Mahdist rising cut ties with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, he turned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a>, whose officers he supplied with men and provisions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The 1894 Franco-Congolese agreement placed the sultanate in the French sphere. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> gradually reduced its rulers' authority, and the sultanate was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ubangi-shari">Ubangi-Shari</a> by about 1913.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1870 CE – 1913 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.92%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1870 CE – 1913 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Zemio</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zemio</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pazande</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/central-african-republic">Central African Republic</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Zemio</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1892&amp;focus=sultanate-of-zemio" aria-label="Sultanate of Zemio on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5377 1989 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Zemio lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5697 2245L5515 2270"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5515 2270h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5697 2245h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5697 2245h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Zemio. <a href="/atlas?year=1892&amp;focus=sultanate-of-zemio">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

